  "analysis": "We need to compute the area swept by rotating a polygon around a point P outside it. The region cleared is the set of all points with distance from P between the minimum and maximum distances that points of the polygon can have to P during the rotation. This equals a full annulus with inner radius r and outer radius R, where:\n- R is the maximum distance from P to any point of the polygon. Since the distance to P is a convex function along any segment, the maximum over the polygon occurs at a vertex. So R^2 = max over vertices of |P - Vi|^2.\n- r is the minimum distance from P to any point of the polygon (including boundary). This is achieved on the boundary: the minimum distance from a point to a polygon equals the minimum distance to its edges (segments). For each edge AB, compute the distance from P to the segment AB (clamped projection). r^2 is the minimum of these distances squared.\nThe area is then: area = pi * (R^2 - r^2).\nImplementation plan:\n- Read n and P, polygon vertices.\n- Compute R^2 as the maximum squared distance from P to each vertex.\n- For each edge AB, compute the squared distance from P to the segment AB using projection clamped to [0,1]. Keep the minimum as r^2.\n- Output pi * (R^2 - r^2) with high precision.\nEdge cases handled: P strictly outside guarantees r > 0. Use long double for precision; print with sufficient digits.\n",
  "plan": "1) Implement a C++17 program:\n   - Read n, Px, Py and the n vertices.\n   - Compute R2 as the maximum squared distance from P to vertices.\n   - For each edge (i to i+1 mod n), compute distance from P to the segment using projection:\n       t = dot(P-A, B-A) / |B-A|^2; clamp t to [0,1]; closest point = A + t*(B-A);\n       d2 = |P - closest|^2; update r2 as the minimum d2 across edges.\n   - pi = acosl(-1.0L); area = pi*(R2 - r2).\n   - Print with 15+ digits after decimal.\n2) Compile and test with sample inputs to verify correctness.\n3) Provide the exact commands to create the file, compile, and run samples.\n",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > main.cpp <<'CPP'\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main(){\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n; long long px, py;\n    if(!(cin>>n>>px>>py)) return 0;\n    vector<pair<long long,long long>> a(n);\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){ long long x,y; cin>>x>>y; a[i]={x,y}; }\n\n    long double R2 = 0.0L; // max distance^2 to vertices\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){\n        long double dx = (long double)a[i].first - (long double)px;\n        long double dy = (long double)a[i].second - (long double)py;\n        long double d2 = dx*dx + dy*dy;\n        if(d2 > R2) R2 = d2;\n    }\n\n    long double r2 = numeric_limits<long double>::infinity();\n    for(int i=0;i<n;i++){\n        auto A = a[i]; auto B = a[(i+1)%n];\n        long double ax = (long double)A.first, ay = (long double)A.second;\n        long double bx = (long double)B.first, by = (long double)B.second;\n        long double ABx = bx - ax, ABy = by - ay;\n        long double APx = (long double)px - ax, APy = (long double)py - ay; // vector from A to P\n        long double denom = ABx*ABx + ABy*ABy;\n        long double t = 0.0L;\n        if(denom > 0){ t = (APx*ABx + APy*ABy) / denom; if(t<0) t=0; if(t>1) t=1; }\n        long double cx = ax + t*ABx; long double cy = ay + t*ABy;\n        long double dx = (long double)px - cx, dy = (long double)py - cy;\n        long double d2 = dx*dx + dy*dy;\n        if(d2 < r2) r2 = d2;\n    }\n\n    long double pi = acosl(-1.0L);\n    long double area = pi * (R2 - r2);\n\n    cout.setf(std::ios::fixed); cout<<setprecision(15)<<(long double)area<<\"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\nCPP\n\ng++ -std=c++17 -O2 -pipe -static -s -o main main.cpp\n./main << EOF\n3 0 0\n0 1\n-1 2\n1 2\nEOF"
