hich case the x-range is the complement of [tin[v], tout[v]]; this is handled as two ranges: [1, tin[v]-1] and [tout[v]+1, n]).\n  - After collecting all queries, we run them against the 2D segment tree and mark ans[v] = 1 if any query finds a valid S.\n  This yields an O(n log^2 n) solution with memory around O(n log n).\nPlan: implement the above in C++, with an iterative DFS to avoid recursion depth issues, build the 2D segment tree, prepare the queries per vertex, and evaluate them. Finally print the n answers (0/1) separated by spaces.\n",
